  "body": "Sibling of the subagent effort change in 11b9d671c (KorenKrita on Discord). It is left alone there and filed here.\n\nIn the window, Claude Code's subagent effort now sits at the right of the Subagents row, laid out like the tier rows' effort controls. While the subagent model is unset (\"Claude Code picks\"), it shows Default and is disabled. That is because magpie no longer writes an effort without a model: the old code wrote the main model at that effort into `env.CLAUDE_CODE_SUBAGENT_MODEL`, which pinned every subagent to the main model. A saved effort is kept in the stash (`claude.subagent_effort`) and applied when a subagent model is picked.\n\nThe tray panel (`mode === \"panel\"`) still draws its own subagent effort square through `extraField` (internal/gui/assets/app.js, the `extra(f)` branch in the agent row, `SUB_EFFORT`). It is not disabled when no subagent model is set:\n- it shows Default, since `Get` now returns \"\" with no model;\n- it still opens the effort slider;\n- a level picked there is only saved. Nothing reaches Claude Code until a subagent model is set, and the square doesn't say so.\n\nWanted: the panel's square behaves like the window's control while the subagent model is unset. It should be disabled at Default and carry the same title (\"Set a subagent model first: …\"), or be left out of the panel. A GUI test in panel mode should cover it in chromium and webkit.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
